# Parity fixture (cell half) for the Phase 2 bridge's now-removed
# ``-tagged_terms`` experiment -- originally the Task 3 parity corpus.
#
# Identical to struct_tabling.clausal (recursion + compound answers, the
# fixture Task 4's interning measurement depends on) apart from the module
# name -- P3-2 made cells the unconditional compiled representation, so
# both halves compile the same way now, kept as an old-vs-new regression
# anchor.  cons/2 is a declared data functor with no clauses, so every
# ``cons(N, T)`` construction/match lowers to the cell literal
# ``('cons', n, t)``; the atom ``nil`` is an interned str (P3-1's atom
# pivot), same as in every other module.
#
# Self-contained: every functor it constructs or matches is declared here.
-module(struct_tabling_tagged, [
    cons(H, T),
    nil,
    Nats(N, L),
])
-table(Nats/2)

Nats(0, nil),
Nats(N, cons(N, T)) <- (
    N > 0,
    N1 == N - 1,
    Nats(N1, T)
)
